    "why_the_bin_mean_is_used": "the sink is linear in ET_max and nonlinear in the depth, and a steady-state solve holds the depth fixed through the year, so the annual mean of ET_max is the only input the solver can take. The evaporating body is the ground, whose seasonal heat storage is a ground heat flux of a few W/m2 against a net radiation cycle an order larger, so the no-storage end of cv._INTERVAL_BRACKET is the near one rather than a bound",
